WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.026
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 7:
Emotions, Behaviour, and Identity.

2
00:00:05.106 --> 00:00:09.402
In this unit you learn to talk about emotions (how we feel),

3
00:00:09.482 --> 00:00:15.310
behaviour (how we act) and identity (who
we are and where our family comes from).

4
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:21.656
You meet children who feel nervous, curious,
proud and shy, and who learn to be gentle,

5
00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:24.209
polite and generous towards others.

6
00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:31.795
You practise saying how you feel, giving kind advice,
and describing what makes your own family special.

7
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:40.037
By the end you will be ready for the unit story, “The Day
of the Play,” in which Amal finds her courage on stage.

8
00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:46.164
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:54.473
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name many
feelings and describe them, using words like nervous, anxious,

10
00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:55.822
proud, and curious.

11
00:00:55.902 --> 00:01:02.711
You will also describe how people behave, using
words like gentle, selfish, generous, and polite.

12
00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:10.309
You will also talk about experiences in your life using
the present perfect (“I have felt nervous before.”)

13
00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:12.937
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:19.088
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
nervous, anxious, terrified, doubtful, curious, proud.

15
00:01:19.168 --> 00:01:24.071
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:24.151 --> 00:01:27.946
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:28.026 --> 00:01:33.273
The reading sequence includes The Day Before
the Test and Where My Family Comes From.

18
00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:34.151
Read actively.

19
00:01:34.231 --> 00:01:38.475
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:38.555 --> 00:01:42.549
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:42.629 --> 00:01:47.479
The first language focus is Present
Perfect (for life experiences).

22
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:53.660
We use the present perfect for things we
have done or felt at some time in our life,

23
00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.309
when the exact time does not matter.

24
00:01:56.389 --> 00:01:58.148
It links the past to now,

25
00:01:58.228 --> 00:02:05.359
so “I have felt nervous before” tells your listener
that the feeling is part of who you are today.

26
00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:13.379
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:17.333
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: How Do You Feel?

28
00:02:17.413 --> 00:02:21.823
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:21.903 --> 00:02:25.241
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:25.321 --> 00:02:28.793
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:30.387
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:37.247
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:37.327 --> 00:02:40.573
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:48.265
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
